ted trace (5.7).</td>\n251:<tr><td>The <strong>installed head</strong></td>\n257:followed principal, the floor, the installed manifest and the trace:\n272:<tr><td>Sequence at the floor, the installed manifest</td>\n296:  is **abandoned**: `(dao.space.dht/abandon node address)` removes a\n310:  never forgets or abandons a record that is not of its own kind. A\n312:  told so, and succeeds once the head is installed.\n332:`:loaded`; and **the installed head of each followed principal**, read\n334:follower records the installed manifests on the node value;\n339:- Installation replaces the principal's installed manifest in one step.\n359:  followed principal has no installed head parks pending on that\n360:  principal (R10) and is re-checked when its head is installed (R11's\n361:  shape). `(abandon)` and the link policy end it.\n362:- `(yin.head/heads)` answers, per principal, what is installed, the\n373:**Persistence.** The follower's durable state is the last installed\n383:- **Durable before used.** A confirmed head is installed in this order:\n389:     snapshot set, the floor moves, `:installed` is emitted.\n396:  stays installed, and the write is tried again after the node's repair\n411:linked name is what it is today. When an installed head makes a linked\n426:  principal, whether a head is installed.\n447:- A head is installed only after its index is local, its sequence is\n450:- No failure retracts an installed head, and none waits on a clock.\n488:<tr><td><code>(head/judge principal floor installed trace)</code></td>\n521:`dao.space.dht` gains `abandon` and the kind-conflict refusal, and\n523:`:confirmed`, `:installed`, `:refused` (a reason and the trace),\n596:<td>A second ring per followed principal holding the installed trace\n741:  and `forget` keeps its contract.\n758:installed. No trace says how new it is.</td></tr>\n768:<td><code>:yin.head/equivocation</code>; the installed head stays.</td>\n771:<td>Nothing. The installed head stays.</td>\n","exit_code":